---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'; import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro'; import RelatedTools from '../../components/RelatedTools.astro'; import JsonLd from '../../components/seo/JsonLd.astro'; import { absoluteUrl } from '../../config'; const title='How to Test a Mouse Scroll Wheel'; const description='A practical step-by-step process for testing mouse wheel direction, jumping, and inconsistent scrolling.';
---
<BaseLayout {title} {description} path="/guides/how-to-test-mouse-wheel" type="article"><JsonLd data={{'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'Article',headline:title,description,url:absoluteUrl('/guides/how-to-test-mouse-wheel')}}/><Breadcrumbs items={[{label:'Guides',href:'/guides/how-to-test-mouse-wheel'},{label:'How to Test a Mouse Wheel'}]}/><article class="content"><h1>{title}</h1><p class="lead">The most useful wheel test is repeatable: test one direction at a time, then compare the same mouse in a different browser or computer.</p><h2>1. Run a browser test</h2><p>Open the <a href="/">Scroll Wheel Test</a>, select Up or Down, and roll steadily in the test area for five to ten seconds. Collect at least 20 events before judging the result.</p><h2>2. Repeat and compare</h2><p>Repeat the test in the other direction. Then try another browser. A problem that appears only in one application may not be caused by the mouse itself.</p><h2>3. Check the connection</h2><p>For wireless mice, charge or replace the battery and position the receiver nearby. For wired mice, reconnect the cable and try another port. Avoid making several changes at once; otherwise you will not know which helped.</p><h2>4. Test another device</h2><p>Try your mouse on another PC, or use a known-good mouse on the same PC. This is often the clearest way to distinguish mouse, receiver, and system settings.</p><h2>5. Review settings and hardware</h2><p>Check operating-system and manufacturer software settings. If the pattern follows the mouse, review the maker’s cleaning or support guidance before attempting a repair.</p><p>For a visual baseline, run the <a href="/">Scroll Wheel Test</a> again after each meaningful change.</p><RelatedTools current="wheel"/></article></BaseLayout>
